  "note": "Each model is a rigged, animated skeletal mesh (own skeleton, walk/run/idle/eat/death clips) imported to /Game/Rim3D/Generated/Animals/<model>. `lengthM` is each model's real nose-to-tail length in metres (U15 fits the imported mesh to it, the import is about 3 times too big); `scale` is the multiplier on that size for the def's body size; a def with no real model yet is under `missing` and is drawn as the husky. Retargeting onto shared skeletons is left for U15.",
  "lengthM": {"Alpaca": 1.4, "Bull": 2.5, "Cow": 2.3, "Deer": 1.7, "Donkey": 1.9, "Fox": 0.9, "Horse": 2.4, "Horse_White": 2.4, "Husky": 1.0, "ShibaInu": 0.8, "Stag": 1.9, "Wolf": 1.3, "TRex": 12.0, "Raptor": 3.5, "Buffalo": 2.9, "WildBear": 2.2, "WildElk": 2.3, "WildDoe": 1.6, "WildMountainGoat": 1.5, "WildBighorn": 1.6, "WildGoose": 0.9, "WildGuineafowl": 0.55, "WildFox": 0.9, "WildBuffalo": 3.0, "Turkey": 1.1, "Camel": 3.0, "Iguana": 1.5, "Capybara": 1.2, "WolfSpider": 2.0, "RhinoBeetle": 0.6},
  "models": ["Alpaca", "Bull", "Cow", "Deer", "Donkey", "Fox", "Horse", "Horse_White", "Husky", "ShibaInu", "Stag", "Wolf"],
  "importsNote": "Realistic rigged Sketchfab models (sneed's downloads, assets/raw/sketchfab on the PC, not in Git). The AnimalArt commandlet imports each `file` (glTF, real size, so no lengthM) and renames the clips named in `clips` to <model>AnimalArmature_<role>, the names the game looks for. `yaw` turns the mesh to face the actor's forward (the Quaternius models need -90); `walkCm` and `gallopCm` are how far the walk and gallop clips go per second at scale 1. A model with no Death clip lies on its side, still, when it dies. `\"fit\": \"pose\"` (Sketchfab's FBX conversions, whose mesh bounds are in another unit than their animation) fits `lengthM` to the skeleton in the idle pose instead of the mesh's bounds. Entries with `assets` (object paths by role, plus `parts` drawn on the body's pose) are packs already in Unreal's format, copied into game/Content (the African Animals Pack: game/Content/AfricanAnimalsPack, not in Git); the commandlet skips them.",
