    {"model": "Raptor", "file": "assets/raw/fab/pbr-velociraptor-animated/source/RaptorSF/Raptor/Raptor_Animated_FBX.fbx", "credit": "PBR Velociraptor (Animated) by Ferocious Industries, Fab Standard License (sneed's library)", "clips": {"Idle": "Raptor_Idle1_Anim_RaptorArmature_", "Walk": "Raptor_Walk_Anim_RaptorArmature_R", "Gallop": "Raptor_Run1_Anim_RaptorArmature_R", "Eating": "Raptor_EatPrey_Anim_RaptorArmatur", "Death": "Raptor_Death1_Anim_RaptorArmature"}, "yaw": -90, "albedo": "assets/raw/fab/pbr-velociraptor-animated/source/RaptorSF/Raptor/Textures/Raptor_PatternC_Albedo.png", "walkCm": 100, "gallopCm": 400, "note": "The FBX from source/RaptorSF.zip (unzipped there). Interchange cuts the clip names short (Raptor_Animated_FBXRaptorArmature_RaptorArmature_RaptorArmature_<clip>_RaptorArmature..., about 100 characters), hence the odd endings. 34 clips incl. Bite, Roar, Leap, Sleep; _RM ones have root motion. The Rulo velociraptor.glb has no animations, not used. `albedo` imports Pattern C (brown) as the body colour and moves the materials onto a copy of the engine FBX master with skeletal and morph-target usage flags (without them the game drew the default material, a black raptor)."},
    {"model": "Buffalo", "file": "assets/raw/fab/buffalo-a1/FbxBlender/FbxBlender/Buffalo_A1.Fbx", "credit": "Buffalo_A1 by Animated3D, CC BY, free on Fab", "clips": {"Idle": "Idle", "Death": "Die"}, "yaw": -90, "walkCm": 120, "gallopCm": 450, "note": "source.zip unzipped in assets/raw/fab/buffalo-a1 (FbxBlender.zip, all motions in one file). The free version has only Idle, Die, Lying and Turnleft: no walk or run, so it walks and runs on its idle (the game falls back on it) and slides. Textures are embedded in the FBX; its material goes on the skinned copy of the FBX master like every FBX import."},
